AutoAnatomy strips TotalSegmentator down to its head_muscles and
headneck_muscles tasks and adds a new Textual-based terminal GUI and
headless CLI on top of the retained nnU-Net inference engine. Its primary
task, dental_segmentator, runs an independently published DentalSegmentator
checkpoint (Dot et al., J Dentistry 2024; CC-BY 4.0) rather than an upstream
TotalSegmentator task.

The headneck_muscles task (upstream TotalSegmentator task_ids 778/779)
requires a license for commercial use (free for non-commercial use). Contact
Jakob Wasserthal (jakob.wasserthal@usb.ch) for a commercial license.
dental_segmentator and head_muscles require no license for either use.

See LICENSE for the full Apache 2.0 license text.

Auto3DSeg integration
--------------------
The auto3dseg_muscles task uses MONAI's SegResNetDS architecture and the
Whole Head Segmentation 0.5 mm v1.0.1 checkpoint published by the
SlicerMONAIAuto3DSeg contributors (Andras Lasso, Andres Diaz-Pinto and
contributors). Philippe Pellerin contributed the masticatory annotation
work described in the associated Slicer community discussion.

MONAI: https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI (Apache-2.0).
Slicer extension and reference inference implementation:
https://github.com/lassoan/SlicerMONAIAuto3DSeg (MIT).
The MIT notice is preserved in
autoanatomy/engine/resources/SlicerMONAIAuto3DSeg-LICENSE.txt.
Checkpoint source:
https://github.com/lassoan/SlicerMONAIAuto3DSeg/releases/download/Models/whole-head-05mm-v1.0.1.zip

The model weights are downloaded from their original publisher and are not
included in AutoAnatomy's source or wheel. The publisher's model registry
does not state a separate license for this checkpoint; AutoAnatomy's
Apache-2.0 license does not grant rights to third-party weights or their
training data. Consult the publisher for the applicable checkpoint terms.
